WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.723
Time of day strongly affects thermal patterns.

00:00:02.723 --> 00:00:04.971
Sunlight warms surfaces at different rates,

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:07.969
and materials release stored heat differently after sunset.

00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:12.840
A warm roof area may reflect solar loading rather than an active defect.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.837
Wind cools surfaces and can reduce temperature differences.

00:00:15.837 --> 00:00:21.083
Rain, fog, and humidity alter heat transfer and may reduce effective range or contrast.

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:26.704
Water on a surface can change emissivity and create patterns unrelated to the suspected condition.

00:00:26.704 --> 00:00:30.451
Surface material, finish, angle, and texture affect emission and reflection.

00:00:30.451 --> 00:00:33.448
Shiny metal may reflect a nearby heat source.

00:00:33.448 --> 00:00:37.945
Glass may behave as a reflective or opaque surface in the thermal

00:00:37.945 --> 00:00:40.942
band rather than revealing what is behind it.

00:00:40.942 --> 00:00:44.689
Terrain and geometry create shadowing, exposure, drainage, and airflow differences.

00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:46.563
Seasonal vegetation, snow, soil moisture,

00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:51.059
and recent weather change the background against which an anomaly is judged.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:54.432
Environmental history matters, not only conditions at capture time.

00:00:54.432 --> 00:00:58.179
Recent sun, heating or cooling cycles, rain, equipment load, occupancy,

00:00:58.179 --> 00:01:03.050
and shutdown can determine whether a target has reached a useful thermal state.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.296
Interior and exterior temperature difference can also determine whether a building pattern is visible.

00:01:08.296 --> 00:01:12.043
If the thermal driving force is weak or changing rapidly,

00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:16.164
a negative result may simply mean the collection conditions were unsuitable.

00:01:16.164 --> 00:01:20.286
Document temperature, wind, precipitation, humidity, sun, time, target state, distance, angle,

00:01:20.286 --> 00:01:21.785
and relevant recent conditions.

00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:24.408
If the environment cannot produce meaningful contrast,

00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:27.780
reschedule instead of forcing an interpretation from weak data.
